    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "mssql",
        "uid": "xLTWsaF7k"
      },
      "description": "In the context of a WSUS (Windows Server Update Services) server, the terms \"Arrival Date\" and \"Creation Date\" refer to different aspects of an update:\n\n1. **Arrival Date**: \n    - This is the date when the update was actually received by your WSUS server.\n    - It indicates when the update became available to the WSUS server from Microsoft's update servers.\n    - This date is important for WSUS administrators because it helps in tracking when new updates are brought into the WSUS system.\n    - It's useful for understanding the timeline of updates availability within your WSUS infrastructure.\n\n\n2. **Creation Date**:\n    - This refers to the date when the update was originally created by Microsoft.\n    - It's the date when the update was finalized and made ready for distribution.\n    - The Creation Date is important for understanding the age of the update and for some administrative purposes, like coordinating updates with known issues or release notes published by Microsoft.\n",
